{"tool_name":"doubletd","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"doubletd","home":"https://github.com/elkebir-group/doubletD","summary":"Detecting doublets in single-cell DNA sequencing data.","addition_date":"2021-11-27T16:51:28.990076Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-27T16:51:28.992770Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:doubletd","credit":[{"email":"melkebir@illinois.edu","name":"Mohammed El-Kebir","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Amplification detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3965"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"doubletD","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAB266","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 The Author(s) 2021. Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: While single-cell DNA sequencing (scDNA-seq) has enabled the study of intratumor heterogeneity at an unprecedented resolution, current technologies are error-prone and often result in doublets where two or more cells are mistaken for a single cell. Not only do doublets confound downstream analyses, but the increase in doublet rate is also a major bottleneck preventing higher throughput with current single-cell technologies. Although doublet detection and removal are standard practice in scRNA-seq data analysis, options for scDNA-seq data are limited. Current methods attempt to detect doublets while also performing complex downstream analyses tasks, leading to decreased efficiency and/or performance. Results: We present doubletD, the first standalone method for detecting doublets in scDNA-seq data. Underlying our method is a simple maximum likelihood approach with a closed-form solution. We demonstrate the performance of doubletD on simulated data as well as real datasets, outperforming current methods for downstream analysis of scDNA-seq data that jointly infer doublets as well as standalone approaches for doublet detection in scRNA-seq data. Incorporating doubletD in scDNA-seq analysis pipelines will reduce complexity and lead to more accurate results.","authors":[{"name":"El-Kebir M."},{"name":"Sashittal P."},{"name":"Weber L.L."}],"date":"2021-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"DoubletD: Detecting doublets in single-cell DNA sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC8275324","pmid":"34252961"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Phylogeny","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0084"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"doubletD","home":"https://bio.tools/doubletd","summary":"Detecting doublets in single-cell DNA sequencing data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:doubletd/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":12,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2025"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":5,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab266","pmcid":"PMC8275324","pmid":"34252961","ref_count":32,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2017"},{"count":3,"year":"2018"},{"count":6,"year":"2016"},{"count":8,"year":"2019"},{"count":9,"y